WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:05.425
Lab 1 runs in the kit's servicenow-sailpoint
folder, with no tenant.

3
00:00:05.425 --> 00:00:09.125
Step one runs the re-read
tests, and fifteen pass.

4
00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:13.151
Step two runs the client offline
over the six waiting records,

5
00:00:13.151 --> 00:00:16.150
with the clock fixed at
noon on November first.

6
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.300
Read the output.

7
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.712
Three records verify, and the client
would patch each one to closed.

8
00:00:21.712 --> 00:00:26.737
The terminated user is a mismatch: the
intended state says account enabled false,

9
00:00:26.737 --> 00:00:31.237
and the read says true, so the client
would reopen it with that difference.

10
00:00:31.237 --> 00:00:36.004
The third record is pending, because
the ISC copy predates the change,

11
00:00:36.004 --> 00:00:38.513
so re-run after the next aggregation.

12
00:00:38.513 --> 00:00:43.875
The fifth is skipped, because its intended
state names nothing a re-read can check.

13
00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:46.737
Every line says what the
client would do and why.

14
00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:48.872
It's a dry run, so nothing is written,

15
00:00:48.872 --> 00:00:52.130
and pending and skipped
records are never patched.
